# Docs

## Voice (override caveman for docs)

Normal professional language for all documentation output.
Zero draft voice. Zero AI meta-commentary. Zero references to "me" or the AI.
Publishable externally as-is.

## Standards

- External docs: polished, technical depth, semi-technical overview when needed.
- Internal docs/specs: concise, dense, engineer-to-engineer. Not slop.
- READMEs: short, structured — what it does, how to run, env vars needed.
- Plan files: preserve structure. Mark sections DONE. Don't remove preservation notes.

## Formatting

- Tables over prose for structured data.
- Respect terse artifact requests ("two tables, nothing else" = literally that).
- Commit messages: conventional, imperative, concise.
- PR descriptions: clean, informative, match repo conventions.

## Constraints

- Canonical docs (project contracts, plan files) = don't edit unless told.
- No generated documentation longer than needed. Density > length.
- No placeholder content. Encode operational truths.
